From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:24:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] iio: qcom_smgr: let the core demux partial 3-axis scans

The report handler always pushes X, Y and Z of an accelerometer,
gyroscope or magnetometer sample in that order, which is the scan layout
only when all three channels are enabled. A buffer with fewer axes
enabled (in_accel_z_en alone, say) got X where it expected its first
enabled channel.

Declare the full mask as the only available scan mask of the 3-axis
devices, so that the IIO core enables all three axes and copies out the
channels each buffer asked for. The single-channel devices need nothing.

The driver is in the msm8996-mainline tree (v6.19.5-msm8996), not in
mainline yet.

Tested on a Galaxy Tab S3 (SM-T820) with all three axes enabled, which
is what iio-sensor-proxy does: samples unchanged. Scans with fewer axes
are untested.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
index b4f016bdab50..3f753c02a648 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2021-2025, Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
  */
 
+#include <linux/bits.h>
 #include <linux/iio/buffer.h>
 #include <linux/iio/common/qcom_smgr.h>
 #include <linux/iio/iio.h>
@@ -712,6 +713,12 @@ static const struct iio_chan_spec qcom_smgr_pressure_iio_channels[] = {
 	}
 };
 
+/*
+ * The report handler always pushes all three axes of a 3-axis sensor; let
+ * the IIO core pick out the channels a buffer has enabled.
+ */
+static const unsigned long qcom_smgr_xyz_scan_masks[] = { GENMASK(2, 0), 0 };
+
 static const char *const qcom_smgr_sensor_type_device_names[] = {
 	[SNS_SMGR_SENSOR_TYPE_ACCEL] = "qcom-smgr-accel",
 	[SNS_SMGR_SENSOR_TYPE_GYRO] = "qcom-smgr-gyro",
@@ -769,6 +776,16 @@ static int qcom_smgr_register_sensor(struct qcom_smgr *smgr,
 		iio_dev->num_channels = qcom_smgr_sensor_type_num_channels[sensor->type];
 	}
 
+	switch (sensor->type) {
+	case SNS_SMGR_SENSOR_TYPE_ACCEL:
+	case SNS_SMGR_SENSOR_TYPE_GYRO:
+	case SNS_SMGR_SENSOR_TYPE_MAG:
+		iio_dev->available_scan_masks = qcom_smgr_xyz_scan_masks;
+		break;
+	default:
+		break;
+	}
+
 	sensor->iio_dev = iio_dev;
 
 	ret = devm_iio_kfifo_buffer_setup(smgr->dev, iio_dev,
-- 
